  "summary": "n8n helper package exfiltrates host recon to attacker domain on install and import",
  "details": "package.json declares a postinstall script that runs `id`, `hostname`, `uname -a`, and lists `/home`, base64-encodes the output, and POSTs it via `curl -sk` (TLS verification disabled) to https://jasabersama.id/portfolio-data.php. The same host reconnaissance and exfiltration is repeated at module load time from the package `main` (index.js) via `child_process.execSync` + curl, so any tool that requires/imports the package (e.g. n8n startup) re-triggers the beacon. A bundled n8n node at nodes/PwnNode.node.js exposes the same recon as an executable node returning `{ pwned: true, result: <output> }` and writes marker files to /tmp/n8n_pwned_local.txt and /tmp/n8n_rce_result.txt, confirming the package is a proof-of-concept attack payload rather than a legitimate helper utility.",
